-- A named site takes a rule's TYPICALLY default unless the name is an OVERLOAD
-- of that rule (not-ok/tc/typically-overloaded-site.l4). Three things that look
-- like an overload and are not, because each is decided by the site alone:
--
--   1. a record field that shares the rule's name (a field takes no named inputs);
--   2. a bare definition that shares the rule's name (it takes only a section
--      GIVEN, and the site names an input of the rule);
--   3. an earlier site that did have to choose between two overloads (the choice
--      must not follow the rule to the sites below it).

§ `A field of the same name`

DECLARE Order HAS
    discount IS A NUMBER

GIVEN price IS A NUMBER
      rate  IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 0.1
GIVETH A NUMBER
discount MEANS price TIMES rate

#EVAL discount WITH price IS 100                  -- 10: the rate takes its default
#EVAL discount WITH price IS 100, rate IS 0.2     -- 20

§ `A bare definition of the same name`

fee MEANS 7

GIVEN price IS A NUMBER
      rate  IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 0.2
GIVETH A NUMBER
fee MEANS price TIMES rate

#EVAL fee WITH price IS 100                       -- 20
#EVAL fee WITH price IS 100, rate IS 0.5          -- 50

§ `Pricing`

GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

§ `Other`

GIVEN base   IS A STRING
      factor IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
scaled MEANS base

§ `Use`

#EVAL scaled WITH base IS 10, rate IS 2           -- 20: chosen among the two, every input written
#EVAL `Pricing`.scaled WITH base IS 10            -- 30: one candidate, so its default is taken
#EVAL scaled WITH base IS 10, rate IS 5           -- 50: and the site above did not take the rule's default away
